ath12k: qmi: give the firmware the caldb region the DT describes

ath12k answers a CALDB_MEM_REGION_TYPE memory request with paddr = 0,
on the grounds that it does not drive cold boot calibration itself.

Vendor firmware does it anyway. With a null address it has nowhere to
put the result -- RAM starts at 0x40000000 on IPQ5332 -- and the Q6
reports a fatal error a few hundred milliseconds after the QMI
handshake:

  ath12k_ahb c000000.wifi: chip_id 0x0 chip_family 0xb board_id 0xff
  qcom-q6-mpd d100000.remoteproc: fatal error without message
  remoteproc remoteproc0: crash detected in d100000.remoteproc

The device tree already describes the region: ipq5332.dtsi gives the
wifi node memory-region = <&q6_ipq5332_data>, <&m3_dump>, <&q6_caldb>,
<&mlo_global_mem>, and index 2 is exactly what is wanted here. The M3
dump case a few lines below already takes index 1 the same way.

Boards without a caldb region keep the old behaviour rather than
failing to probe.

This is a local patch: upstream would need to decide whether ath12k
should describe this memory when it does not use the results itself.

Signed-off-by: Hideo Sumi <hideo.sumi@mugops.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
@@ -2752,13 +2752,33 @@
 			idx++;
 			break;
 		case CALDB_MEM_REGION_TYPE:
-			/* Cold boot calibration is not enabled in Ath12k. Hence,
-			 * assign paddr = 0.
-			 * Once cold boot calibration is enabled add support to
-			 * assign reserved memory from DT.
+			/* Hand the firmware the caldb region the device tree
+			 * already describes, rather than a null address.
+			 *
+			 * Upstream passes 0 here because ath12k does not drive
+			 * cold boot calibration itself. Vendor firmware does it
+			 * anyway, and with paddr = 0 it has nowhere to put the
+			 * result -- RAM starts at 0x40000000 on this SoC -- so
+			 * the Q6 reports a fatal error shortly after the QMI
+			 * handshake and takes the radio down with it.
+			 *
+			 * If the board has no caldb region, fall back to the
+			 * old behaviour rather than failing the probe.
 			 */
-			ab->qmi.target_mem[idx].paddr = 0;
-			ab->qmi.target_mem[idx].v.ioaddr = NULL;
+			rmem = ath12k_core_get_reserved_mem(ab, 2);
+			if (rmem && rmem->size >= ab->qmi.target_mem[i].size) {
+				ab->qmi.target_mem[idx].paddr = rmem->base;
+				ab->qmi.target_mem[idx].v.ioaddr =
+					ioremap(ab->qmi.target_mem[idx].paddr,
+						ab->qmi.target_mem[i].size);
+				if (!ab->qmi.target_mem[idx].v.ioaddr) {
+					ret = -EIO;
+					goto out;
+				}
+			} else {
+				ab->qmi.target_mem[idx].paddr = 0;
+				ab->qmi.target_mem[idx].v.ioaddr = NULL;
+			}
 			ab->qmi.target_mem[idx].size = ab->qmi.target_mem[i].size;
 			ab->qmi.target_mem[idx].type = ab->qmi.target_mem[i].type;
 			idx++;
